  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Investor Anthony Medich approached the refurbishment of Hotel Centennial as a neighbourhood project. He wanted the interiors to fit the surrounding homes of Woollahra and drew inspiration from Soho House clubs. Designers Luchetti Krelle created the fit-out, combining the building's history with contemporary furnishings.\n\nMedich also selected photographs and video works from his own collection for the hotel. Pieces by Rosemary Laing, Destiny Deacon and Shaun Gladwell appeared alongside other contemporary artists. Video art occupied screens that might otherwise have shown sport, while a work by the Japanese collective teamLab brought changing seasonal imagery to the library.",
